WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.732
QMB PRISM is the Platform for Review, Improvement and Strategic Monitoring at Symbiosis International University.

2
00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:14.536
Developed by Doctor Dharmendra Pandey, it connects quarterly QIC meetings, institutional data, action tracking, and quality scores.

3
00:00:14.536 --> 00:00:23.174
My contribution was suggesting institutional and research data, proposing the marking-system concept, and testing the workflow across user roles.

4
00:00:23.174 --> 00:00:28.059
I currently administer the portal and handle correction requests and user queries.

5
00:00:28.759 --> 00:00:35.836
I tested the portal by following the workflow as an institute QIC coordinator, then a Quality Mentor, and then an administrator.

6
00:00:35.836 --> 00:00:43.357
This included creating meetings, locking the agenda, preparing Minutes of Meeting, reviewing the submission, and testing mentor marking.

7
00:00:43.357 --> 00:00:52.093
Moving through these roles let me check the workflow as different users would experience it, including the handover from institute coordination to QMB review.

8
00:00:52.793 --> 00:00:57.337
I suggested including institutional data and research information in the portal.

9
00:00:57.337 --> 00:01:04.833
The documented system collects quarterly figures covering faculty and students, research output, sponsored projects, and placements.

10
00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:08.127
Designated research fields are supplied centrally by SCRI.

11
00:01:08.127 --> 00:01:13.125
This puts supporting institutional information alongside the meeting and review process.

12
00:01:13.125 --> 00:01:19.032
My contribution was the requirements suggestion; the portal implementation was handled by the developer.

13
00:01:19.732 --> 00:01:25.823
I proposed introducing a marking system because it would help management see how institutes were progressing.

14
00:01:25.823 --> 00:01:37.558
The documented portal uses a quarterly quality score with forty points for process compliance, forty for outcomes, and twenty for the Quality Mentor assessment, with additional rules for exceptions and bonuses.

15
00:01:37.558 --> 00:01:40.352
My contribution was proposing the scoring concept.

16
00:01:40.352 --> 00:01:44.431
I do not claim authorship of the detailed criteria, formulas, or weights.

17
00:01:45.131 --> 00:01:50.366
I currently handle the portal as an administrator, responding to corrections and queries.

18
00:01:50.366 --> 00:01:56.423
My testing experience across coordinator, mentor, and admin roles helps me understand the user journey.

19
00:01:56.423 --> 00:02:02.246
The wider portal supports meeting records, mentor review, action follow-up, and progress reporting.

20
00:02:02.246 --> 00:02:10.185
My ongoing contribution is operational administration and user support, alongside the requirements input and testing already described.

21
00:02:10.885 --> 00:02:22.215
This project demonstrates my contribution to defining institutional reporting needs, proposing a management-oriented scoring concept, testing a multi-role workflow, and supporting a portal in daily use.

22
00:02:22.215 --> 00:02:25.412
Development credit remains with Doctor Dharmendra Pandey.

23
00:02:25.412 --> 00:02:31.357
My role is represented as a requirements contributor, functional tester, and current portal administrator.

24
00:02:31.357 --> 00:02:36.125
Illustrations in this case study do not reproduce confidential institutional records.
